@host = http://localhost:8080

### What is this app running right now (store, cache, discovery, options)?
GET {{host}}/config
Accept: application/json

### Every persisted task row with its state, priority and next run
GET {{host}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

### Every registered DEFINITION, incl. never-run / manual / enqueue-only ones (with Description)
GET {{host}}/registered
Accept: application/json

### Only the scheduled ones (states: Idle, Scheduled, Queued, Running, Completed, Failed, Cancelled)
GET {{host}}/tasks?state=Scheduled&limit=100
Accept: application/json

### A single task
GET {{host}}/tasks/attr:heartbeat
Accept: application/json

### Execution history for a task, newest first (needs CRONNER_EXEC_HISTORY>0). Each run records a
### Running row on start, finalized to Succeeded/Failed/Cancelled when it ends.
GET {{host}}/tasks/attr:heartbeat/history?take=20
Accept: application/json

### Trigger the manual attribute task (it has no cron string, so this is the only way it runs)
POST {{host}}/tasks/attr:manual/run

### Trigger the manual lambda task
POST {{host}}/tasks/lambda:manual/run

# ─── One-off jobs: enqueue with a typed payload ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Enqueue a one-off with a payload (the payload lands as the job's method parameter)
POST {{host}}/enqueue/notify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "to": "alice@example.com", "message": "your import finished", "attempt": 1 }

### Bodyless is fine too — the endpoint falls back to a demo payload (never enqueues null)
POST {{host}}/enqueue/notify

### ... watch the one-off deliver its payload and complete
GET {{host}}/activity?take=20&jobId=enqueue:notify
Accept: application/json

# ─── Execution lock: keepalive, loss, cancellation ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### Keepalive: a 35s run with LockTtl=20s — expect OnLockAcquire, ~3x OnKeepAlive, then OnLockRelease
POST {{host}}/tasks/lock:keepalive/run

### ... watch the lock events
GET {{host}}/activity?take=20&jobId=lock:keepalive
Accept: application/json

### Measured renewal cadence vs. the expected LockTtl/2.
### Set CRONNER_SLOW_KEEPALIVE_MS above LockTtl/2 (e.g. 15000) and run lock:keepalive again:
### the gaps must stay at LockTtl/2, because keepalive hooks are fired detached from the renewal loop.
GET {{host}}/locks
Accept: application/json

### Lock loss, step 1: start the stealable long run
POST {{host}}/tasks/lock:stealable/run

### Lock loss, step 2: take its claim away (the lock is released on its owner's behalf, as a reclaim by
### another node would) — the next keepalive is refused, the run is cancelled, OnLockLost fires
POST {{host}}/tasks/lock:stealable/steal-lock

### ... watch it stand down; its history row ends Cancelled with CronnerExecutionErrors.LockLost
GET {{host}}/activity?take=20&jobId=lock:stealable
Accept: application/json

### The lease rule, step 1 (CRONNER_STORE=custom only): start the long run
POST {{host}}/tasks/lock:outage/run

### The lease rule, step 2a — a SHORT outage (renewals throw for 5s under a 20s TTL): the run SURVIVES.
### /activity shows "[store] lock renewal THREW" a few times, then a successful keepalive.
POST {{host}}/store/renewal-outage?seconds=5

### The lease rule, step 2b — a LONG outage (renewals throw for 60s): the engine abandons the run BEFORE its
### lease lapses (OnLockLost, history row Cancelled + LockLost), so no other instance could ever overlap it.
POST {{host}}/store/renewal-outage?seconds=60

### ... watch it
GET {{host}}/activity?take=30&jobId=lock:outage
Accept: application/json

### The execution id: lock:keepalive names a per-run log file after ICronnerJobContext.ExecutionId; every hook
### line of that run carries the same id, and it is the Id of the history row below.
GET {{host}}/tasks/lock:keepalive/history?take=5
Accept: application/json

### Cooperative cancellation: start it ...
POST {{host}}/tasks/cancel:long-runner/run

### ... and cancel it (watch the OnCancel hook in /activity and the logs)
POST {{host}}/tasks/cancel:long-runner/cancel

# ─── Progress reporting ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Live progress, rebuilt purely from the progress hooks (total + per-scope)
GET {{host}}/progress
Accept: application/json

### The progress job's own trace (scopes opening, reporting, closing)
GET {{host}}/activity?take=25&jobId=progress:import
Accept: application/json

### Per-schedule hooks (WithHook<T>, expression hooks, delegate) — only ever fire for this task
GET {{host}}/activity?take=25&jobId=progress:reindex
Accept: application/json

### What the expression-style hooks recorded
GET {{host}}/activity?take=25&jobId=hooks:expression
Accept: application/json

# ─── General observation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### What the jobs actually did, newest first
GET {{host}}/activity?take=50
Accept: application/json

### Concurrency policies side by side: drop / queue / parallel
GET {{host}}/activity?take=40&jobId=conc:parallel
Accept: application/json

### Hook-fed counters per task, including the lock events
GET {{host}}/metrics
Accept: application/json

### Liveness
GET {{host}}/healthz
Accept: application/json
